   "title": "Start here",
   "widgets_values": [
    "# LongCat Avatar - Experimental: Start Image to End Image (640)\n\nEXPERIMENTAL, 640 x 640. Starts on the Portrait and steers the final chunk toward the End Image: same person, a different pose, expression or framing. It is a soft pull on the last frame, not a pinned frame; LongCat has no true end-frame input.\n\n**Red nodes are the ones you set.** Everything else runs on its own. The stages run left to right, 1 to 7, each with a note underneath.\n\n1. **Load Portrait** - one person facing the camera, face clearly visible.\n1b. **Load End Image** - the same person as they should look at the very end.\n2. **Load Voiceover** - your speech track, any length.\n3. **Prompt** (optional) - leave empty, or describe the portrait in a sentence.\n4. Run with **batch count 1** to test the first chunk. Check `output/longcat_longform/<name>/chunk_0000.mp4`: lips, face, background.\n5. Run again with a batch count of at least **audio seconds / 3.2**, plus a margin. Each run renders the next unfinished chunk; extra runs are skipped in milliseconds.\n6. The final video lands in `output/`, then the queue is cleared.\n\n**Next video:** load the new voiceover and run. It starts at chunk 1 in its own folder; there is nothing to reset.\n\nA 7-minute voiceover is about 130 chunks. If the batch count box stops at 100, click Run several times: the queue adds up.\n\nFull instructions: https://github.com/tenitsky/longcat-avatar"
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
